Subject: [PATCH 01970/11362] [outer-loop] audit the .393 ARC +44pp
 oracle-distinct win (exp4245): real + leak-free but thin

Operator-requested audit of the headline arc_oracle_distinct_set_encoder_beats_vote.
Findings: (1) LEAKAGE CLEAN -- genuine 5-fold task-level CV (28443 rows), 0 rows where a
task is in its own train set, held-out requires all candidates OOF. (2) NOT cherry-picked --
the 52 held-out tasks ARE the entire available GAP-4 ARC pool (task_n=52), so vote@1=0.25 is
the genuine vote rate, not a wrong-majority-selected subset (my initial selection-inflation
worry was too strong). (3) The +44pp is REAL: the set-encoder recovers 23/30 (77%) wrong-
majority basins vote misses; verifier_is_oracle=false; CI excludes 0.
BUT thin + regime-specific: n=52, wide CI, 58% wrong-majority is a GAP-4-generation property,
OOF over only 52 tasks (no OOD ARC test). So it MOTIVATES the DiffusionGemma bet but doesn't
yet robustly establish 'verifier beats vote on ARC' -- needs more tasks + a fresh task set +
replication (the conductor's A4 replicates only the CODE win, not this ARC one).

